      "Incompatibilists hold that free will and determinism cannot both be true. Hard determinists accept determinism and conclude that we lack free will. Libertarians, in the philosophical sense, hold that we have free will and conclude that determinism is false, at least for human choices. Mere randomness does not obviously help, since a choice caused by chance does not seem to be under the agent's control either.",
